# From "Problem Solving" (Wave II - Threshold, CD1-2). The tape repeats the
# cast-and-wait step three times for verification; written here as two
# passes (first answer, then a check) rather than three near-identical ones.

@segment  problem-solving
@title    Problem Solving
@levels   F12
@duration ~2m30s

say From Focus 12, take the question or problem you brought with you.
pause 5
say Cast it out into your total awareness, and wait for the best answer to come back to you, clearly and distinctly.
pause 15
say You will consciously remember what you receive.
pause 5
say Now repeat it, for clarity. Send the same question out through your entire awareness once more, and wait for the answer.
pause 15
say You will consciously remember and understand the best answer you've received.
pause 6
say At any point in the future, when you're physically wide awake and want the best answer to a question, inhale deeply, pulling fresh energy into your head, and hold your breath. Think the number twelve, then the question.
pause 8
say Exhale, and you'll consciously know the best answer to what you presented.
pause 6
say The more you use this, the easier and more definite it becomes.
pause 6
